:"\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120406\r\n\r\nThey have an index parameter, so this allows changing individual split offsets without needing to use the `split_offsets` array directly.\r\nOriginally I thought `split_offsets[0] = 0` was fine, but its not anymore, and being able to set just one at a time is useful.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n`set_split_offset` and `get_split_offset` were already used in c++ for this purpose.\r\n\r\nThese names were bound to the deprecated `split_offset`, so I had to bind them with different names. They are deprecated getter/setters so I don't think the name matters too much.\r\n\r\nI ran `--validate-extension-api` and it didn't tell me there were any issues even though I am adding a parameter to methods. ~I guess since they are no longer getters/setters its fine?~ Or maybe it just doesn't work locally.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123560/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123560/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}